--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Language models
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Ollin does not bundle, redistribute, or host any language model weights. It runs
against a model that you download yourself using Ollama (https://ollama.com).
Model weights remain subject to their own licenses, which are separate from and
unaffected by Ollin's Apache-2.0 license.

Built with Llama.

Ollin's default configuration uses Meta's Llama 3.2 (3B). Llama 3.2 is licensed
under the Llama 3.2 Community License Agreement, Copyright (c) Meta Platforms,
Inc. All Rights Reserved. Use of Llama 3.2 is additionally subject to Meta's
Acceptable Use Policy: https://www.llama.com/llama3_2/use-policy

    Llama 3.2 Community License:
    https://github.com/meta-llama/llama-models/blob/main/models/llama3_2/LICENSE

Ollin's model is user-configurable (see OLLIN_MODEL in Ollin/config.py). If you
select a different model, that model's license governs your use of it. Note that
licensing can differ between sizes within the same model family — for example,
several Qwen2.5 sizes are Apache-2.0 while Qwen2.5-3B is released under a
non-commercial research license. Check the license for the specific model you
intend to use.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NumPy                 BSD 3-Clause    https://numpy.org
tiktoken              MIT             https://github.com/openai/tiktoken
Ollama (external)     MIT             https://ollama.com
React 18.3.1          MIT            https://react.dev
React DOM 18.3.1      MIT            https://react.dev

React and React DOM are vendored verbatim and unmodified in the application
(`vendor/react*.production.min.js`), which draws the avatar. Their full MIT
license text is reproduced in the application's own NOTICE file, alongside the
LICENSE that their headers refer to. The application bundles no other
third-party code, no web fonts and no CDN scripts.

Ollama is required at runtime but is installed separately by the user and is not
redistributed with Ollin.

The optional Anthropic provider (Ollin/llm.py) uses the `anthropic` Python SDK
(MIT) only if explicitly enabled. It is off by default and is not required.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data sources, attribution and their terms
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Ollin contacts these services only when you ask for the thing they provide.
Naming them in the README's privacy table is a disclosure of what leaves the
machine; this section is the separate obligation — what their licences require
to be said.

OpenStreetMap, via the Overpass API           https://overpass-api.de
    Place and point-of-interest data.
    © OpenStreetMap contributors. Available under the Open Database License
    (ODbL): https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
    Ollin's client leaves at least 3 seconds between calls and caches results
    for an hour, which is inside the OSM operations policies.

Open-Meteo                                    https://open-meteo.com
    Forecasts and place-name geocoding.
    Weather data by Open-Meteo.com, licensed CC-BY 4.0:
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    ⚠️ THE FREE API IS FOR NON-COMMERCIAL USE: "You may only use the free API
    services for non-commercial purposes." Free-tier limits are under 10,000
    calls a day. Ollin's own use is far below that and is non-commercial — but
    Ollin is Apache-2.0, and that licence lets YOU use Ollin commercially. If
    you do, the weather calls become your responsibility: take an Open-Meteo
    paid plan or point the feature elsewhere. This is the same shape as the
    model-licence caution in the README.

Radio Browser                                 https://api.radio-browser.info
    Internet radio station directory.
    Free and open; the project explicitly permits use in "free and non free
    software". It asks for a descriptive User-Agent so operators can see who
    is calling, which `config.USER_AGENT` provides. No attribution required.

Internet Archive                              https://archive.org
    Public-domain film, audio and texts.
    Items carry their OWN licences, which differ per item. Ollin stores and
    displays the licence field it is given rather than assuming public domain.

gpodder.net                                   https://gpodder.net
    Podcast search, via the public directory endpoint `/search.json`.
    No API key and no authentication: the Directory API is documented as
    public content. No attribution is required and no rate limit is published
    — so Ollin imposes its own, leaving a second between calls and caching
    results for an hour, because a community-run free service deserves that
    whether or not it asks. The feed and the audio are fetched from the
    PUBLISHER, not from gpodder.
    The service software (mygpo) is AGPLv3. That covers their server, not an
    HTTP client, so it places no obligation on Ollin.

Ticketmaster Discovery API                    https://developer.ticketmaster.com
    Events. OFF unless you add your own API key, and Ollin ships no key.
    Their API terms of service bind whoever supplies the key, which is you.

Flipp (backflipp.wishabi.com)
    Local store circulars.
    ⚠️ UNDOCUMENTED AND UNPROMISED. This is the backend Flipp's own web app
    talks to: no key, no block, and no published terms either. Ollin
    identifies itself honestly here as everywhere — it does NOT present as a
    browser — and the feature degrades to "I can't see local flyers right now"
    whenever it stops working, which it may at any time.

Apple MapKit / MKDirections / AVSpeechSynthesis
    Routing, local search and the voice, through macOS frameworks on this
    machine. Governed by your macOS and Apple developer terms, not by Ollin's.

RSS feeds
    The headline fetch reads feeds the publisher offers for that purpose.
    Titles and summaries are third-party content, shown as quotations and
    passed through `untrusted.clean` before they reach the model.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Included model state
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Ollin ships a trained phase-field checkpoint. It was trained solely on the seed
corpus authored for this project (Ollin/field/qa_data.py). It contains no
third-party training corpora.
